i used to have a rule that i implemented  for myself no technology within arm's  reach of the bed  however ever since i got an m1 ipad pro  that rule has been absolutely shattered  what's going on guys my name's david  thomas welcome back to the channel today  we're looking at the m1 ipad pro from  somebody who's owned it literally from  day one when it came out if you haven't  seen that video where i talked about the  m1 ipad pro for architects when i first  got it and all the pros and cons i saw  for justifying the purchase i'll link it  up top and down below so you can check  it out but today i wanted to share with  you my long-term thoughts of owning this  device it's been just under six months  now since i received the delivery and  took ownership of the highly expensive  m1 ipad pro and to this day it has been  incredible there definitely has been  some shortfalls which i'll get into a  little bit later on but i wanted to  start with some great news because it  has been the be-all end-all for me  moving in to the apple ecosystem now  like i said in the intro of this video i  used to have that rule no technology  within arm's reach of the bed that meant  no phone no laptop no ipad no nothing  and genuinely i stuck to that rule for  as long as i can remember because still  to this day my phone sits on the other  side of the room plugged in on the floor  because i don't want any distractions  before i go to bed  however the ipad actually completely  shattered this rule and changed the game  for me it is the only device that sits  literally on my bedside table from the  moment i wake up it's picked up and from  the moment i go to bed it's put back  down  it does not leave my side it is the  ultimate all-in-one computer ipad  experience absolutely everything now  from somebody who's been a massive  samsung user and a windows user for so  long i really push myself into not going  down the apple ecosystem unfortunately  for me i bought the m1 ipad pro and am  now contemplating all my other decisions  in life i'm thinking about switching my  samsung s20 ultra to the new iphone i'm  thinking about scrapping this computer  when the new imacs come out in the  larger 27 inch models yet to be  confirmed  but i've just completely changed my  whole way of thinking about technology  because of this simple device  this device genuinely makes everything  so easy i've been able to split it up  into two categories basically dividing  it between personal life and work life  and managing that balance so much better  than i ever could before  previously i'd be carrying around my  laptop and my phone and having my work  emails on one and my personal emails on  one another and then having all my  business essentials on a completely  third device  now i've been able to integrate that so  seamlessly and so smoothly in the m1  ipad pro  and it has been able to handle every  single task i've thrown at it not once  have i had an issue with this ipad as  yet looking at it from a pure  performance beast of a system that's the  genuine reason why i bought the ipad pro  it has been able to stand up to the test  of time i use this thing religiously  throughout the day i'll wake up like i  said i'll pick up my ipad and from about  7 30 till about 9 p.m there'll be some  sort of activity being done on this ipad  either be marking up architectural plans  going through 3d plans with clients or  even doing ar tours with the actual ipad  i'm using a hell of a lot of ram and as  much battery life as i can possibly chew  i don't think there's been a time just  yet where i've completely drained the  battery i have come very very close and  that's because i left it open on my desk  whilst i was working on my computer  absolute max brightness and just left it  on all day it lasted about six hours  before it completely died  but i learned my lesson pretty quick  just simply drag that brightness down to  at least 75  and it lasts forever i think i could  easily use this ipad two days straight  maybe even pushing it to three days  straight of general day-to-day  activities and not have to charge it  which has been a phenomenal advantage  that i didn't even know i really needed  an ipad because i do charge it every  single night but knowing that you're  going to be able to make it through that  entire day with one single charge has  been game changing from the performance  side as well like i said i've been doing  a lot of ar and a lot of vr with this  system the ar capabilities with that  built-in lidar scanner have made it  incredible i'm able to bring up full 3d  models of houses of buildings of  skyscrapers and show them directly in  front of the client and present them  with something that they've never seen  before so it has been really versatile  in all sorts of aspects to be able to  really keep up with the high demand and  high graphics capabilities that i need  personally as an architect now having  said all this there are some slight cons  to the ipad pro  first of all i dropped my ipad pro  outside and it landed smack bang on a  rock  now thank god it did not crack the ipad  has a couple minor scratches somehow  absolute miracle it did not shatter into  a million pieces my heart sank when i  dropped the ipad i was on site doing a  3d lidar scan scanning  an entire environment and actually  creating a video here for youtube  then i slipped fell and dropped the ipad  i genuinely genuinely genuinely thought  i'd be picking that ipad up and looking  at an absolute nightmare of a screen  now i picked it up and to my disbelief  there was literally one tiny tiny  scratch on the screen on the corner  that basically can't even be seen from a  day-to-day operation point of view so  the durability first of all from this  ipad has been phenomenal i'm not one to  go around bashing and beating the ipad  around so i wouldn't really take my  review of durability as the best thing  ever and that you can go around throwing  it  off cliffs and  doing whatever you want with it it still  is a fragile device but it is a lot more  robust than i previously would have  anticipated which is really reassuring  considering the price tag of the device  that was literally one of the only times  that i took it out of the magic keyboard  and used it as an ipad without the magic  keyboard now the magic keyboard for me  is an accessory that i would not go  without it fundamentally changed the  ipad from being just your basic  run-of-the-mill tablet to actually being  able to replace my laptop i do have a  very very high-end laptop that cost  double what this ipad costs  and i never use it ever it literally  sits on the desk next to me never  getting used i've put it up for sale  because  it just doesn't have a purpose anymore  so the ipad has been able to replace  pretty much all of my emails on my phone  all of my emails and all of my work on a  laptop there is one major major major  downside to this ipad pro  and this is just me being pedantic and  me being picky the ipad pro in itself is  ultra light ultra slim and just  phenomenally designed however once you  magnetically click that on to the actual  magic keyboard well all of a sudden that  weight goes through the roof it  literally doubles in overall weight now  in a small little compact package you  wouldn't think too much of it but when  you have to carry this around all day  every day it does become a small little  burden now the simple fact that this  keyboard is just that little bit too  heavy is a bit disappointing  over the last six months because i do  wish that this keyboard was a little bit  lighter the keyboard in itself has  lasted phenomenally well as you see i'll  do a little bit of a b-roll here over  the top of this  the actual surfaces have lasted really  really well it gets thrown into bags  into backpacks it's been on airplanes  it's been in the little luggage  compartments it's been on the car back  seats it's been on site it's been in the  sand it's literally been everywhere that  you would take a regular notebook and a  regular notepad and it survived  everything i've spilled water on it i've  spilled coffee on it there has been some  pretty bad accidents with this ipad but  it survived it all and without a single  fault so far the only thing the ipad has  not been able to replace  is my actual architectural work on a  computer now having said that i do  believe it has the core capabilities  through the ram and the m1 chip to  actually run these programs but  unfortunately these programs aren't  available on a tablet so i can't even go  and test it out all in all would i  recommend the m1 ipad pro six months  after owning it using it every single  day basically religiously and pushing it  to its absolute limits  yes yes i 100 would recommend the ipad  pro i have not had  any genuine issues with this device that  i would go um i wish i didn't buy that  device and coming from me that's  actually a pretty big deal personally i  always buy a device and a couple months  later i go ah you know what  this wasn't the best choice or this  wasn't the best way i could have spent  my money for the first time  genuinely i think the ipad pro with the  m1 chip able to handle so much more than  it ever could before  and genuinely actually do what they  stated in the keynote has been  revolutionary and game changing and on  that note that's all for me today guys  thank you so much for watching i hope  you got the information you were looking  for today and i do hope that the  information i provided at least provided  you with some reassurance that if you're  going to go out and spend a couple  thousand dollars on a tablet at least  you know you're going to be getting your  money's worth if you have any questions  about the ipad pro or anything we've  talked about today check out the links  in the description below there's some  good information some good resources  some discord chat so we can continue  talking about this and there is also the  comments section down below that i  obviously check all the time  if you did enjoy this video please make  sure you smash that like button and the  subscribe button the like button helps  with the youtube algorithm the subscribe  button just genuinely tells me that  you're enjoying this content and you  want to see more of it but that is  genuinely all from me so i'll see you  guys next monday

